// Minting the tokens a client joins with.
//
// This is the call a backend makes most, and the one that decides who anybody
// is. A customer's server authenticates its user however it already does, then
// asks for a token naming that user, that device, that room, and exactly the
// rights they should have. MOQOM never sees the customer's password database
// and never needs to.
//
// The signing key never leaves the control plane. That is the difference from
// the SDK-side token builders this replaces, where the tenant's signing secret
// is shipped into every backend that mints and leaks with any one of them.

